      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the solutions to the equations \\(x + y = 4\\) and \\(3xy = 4\\), we can treat \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) as roots of a quadratic equation. Let the quadratic equation be \\(t^2 - (x+y)t + xy = 0\\). Substituting the given values:\n\\[t^2 - 4t + xy = 0.\\]\nFrom the second equation, \\(3xy = 4\\), we get \\(xy = \\frac{4}{3}\\). Now we have the quadratic equation:\n\\[t^2 - 4t + \\frac{4}{3} = 0.\\]\nTo solve this quadratic equation, we multiply the whole equation by 3 to clear the fraction:\n\\[3t^2 - 12t + 4 = 0.\\]\nWe can solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\(t = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = -12\\), and \\(c = 4\\):\n\\[t = \\frac{-(-12) \\pm \\sqrt{(-12)^2 - 4(3)(4)}}{2(3)} = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{144 - 48}}{6} = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{96}}{6} = \\frac{12 \\pm 4\\sqrt{6}}{6} = \\frac{6 \\pm 2\\sqrt{6}}{3}.\\]\nTherefore, the solutions are:\n\\[x = \\frac{6 + 2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = \\frac{6 - 2\\sqrt{6}}{3}.\\]\nWe can see that these solutions are of the form \\(x = \\frac{a \\pm b\\sqrt{c}}{d}\\) where \\(a = 6\\), \\(b = 2\\), \\(c = 6\\), and \\(d = 3\\). Thus, the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) are 6, 2, 6, and 3 respectively. So the value of \\(a + b + c + d = 6 + 2 + 6 + 3 = 17\\).\n\nThe value of \\(a + b + c + d\\) is \\(\\boxed{17}\\).",
